# Spec-Driven Development

Apply when working in this repo's `docs/` tree or `AGENTS.md`. Read `docs/.sdd.yaml` first.

**The specification — not the code, not the prompt — is the source of truth.** SDD owns the spec/document/traceability layer; exploring, planning, TDD, execution, generic verification, code review, and branch-finishing belong to **superpowers**.

**SDD commands:** `/sdd-scaffold` · `/sdd-specify` · `/sdd-trace` · `/sdd-review` (opt-in, spec-aware review) · `/sdd-archive`. For the full combined flow, superpowers handoffs, and the `docs/superpowers/*` → canonical-tree redirect, use the `spec-driven-development` skill or — in a scaffolded repo — [docs/ai-workflow.md](docs/ai-workflow.md).

**Load-bearing rules:** one canonical home per requirement (index links, spec owns the prose); identifiers immutable once published; don't mix document kinds; don't settle open questions silently (STRAND, ADR, or ask); look domain facts up in the named ground-truth source. No code-first without a `REQ`/spec — `/sdd-specify` first. Route normative content from `docs/superpowers/*` into `docs/specifications/` and land plans in `docs/plans/`. One home per fact in process prose too — commit body / PR body / changelog / review comments cite identifiers rather than restating. Archive the plan **inside the implementing PR** (not a follow-up).
